{"translation": "Ten years, life and death, a vast blank space;
I do not force myself to think of you, yet I cannot forget.
A thousand li away, your lonely grave—
Nowhere to speak of this desolate grief.
Even if we met, you would not know me:
Dust fills my face, my temples are white as frost.
Last night in a dream I suddenly returned to our home;
By the small window, you were doing your hair.
We looked at each other, speechless;
Only the tears flowed in a thousand lines.
I know that year after year, where my heart breaks—
On a moonlit night, the hill of short pines."}

