translation:
The wind is sharp, the sky is high, gibbons wail with sorrow;
The isle is clear, the sand is white, birds wheel and circle there.
Endless, the falling leaves come rustling down;
Unending, the great river rolls on its way.
For miles upon miles, in this sad autumn, I am ever a traveler;
Through all my life, beset by sickness, I climb this terrace alone.
Hardship and bitter regret have filled my temples with frost;
Despairing, I set down my cup of turbid wine.

