translation:
The nation broken, yet hills and streams remain;
Spring in the city, deep the grass and trees.
Moved by the times, flowers splash my tears;
Hating parting, birds startle my heart.
Beacon fires have flared three months unfurled;
A family letter is worth ten thousand gold.
My white hair, scratched, grows ever thinner, shorter—
Soon too scant to hold a single pin.

