translation:
Spring View

The nation is broken, yet mountains and rivers remain;
In spring, the city’s grass and trees grow thick.
Moved by the times, flowers draw tears;
Hating separation, birds alarm the heart.
Beacon fires rage for three months on end;
A letter from home would be worth ten thousand gold.
My white hair, scratched, grows ever thinner—
Almost too scant to hold a hairpin.

