translation:
The capital falls; hills and streams remain;
Spring fills the city, grasses run deep.
Moved by the times, flowers well with tears;
Hating parting birds startle the heart.
Beacon fires burn three months on end;
A single letter from my kin outweighs ten thousand in gold.
I scratch my thinning white hair,
Barely enough left to hold a pin.

