translation:
The wind is sharp, the sky is high, the gibbons wail;
On clear isles, white sands, the birds wheel round and back.
Boundless leaves fall with a rustling, rushing sound;
Endless the Yangtze rolls and surges, coming down.

Ten thousand miles away, grieving at autumn, often a guest;
A hundred years, many sicknesses, I climb this terrace alone.
Hardship and bitter regret have thickened my frost-white temples;
In my destitution, I have just stopped my cup of turbid wine.

