formatted_result:
{"translation": "The state is shattered; hills and streams remain.
Spring in the city; grass and trees grow wild.
Moved by the times, flowers bring forth tears;
Pained by parting, birds alarm the heart.
Beacon fires have burned for three long months;
A letter from home would be worth gold.
I scratch my white hair, it grows ever thinner,
Soon too short to hold a pin."}

