The nation is shattered, mountains and rivers remain;
The city in spring, grass and trees grow wild.
Moved by the times, flowers draw my tears;
Hating separation, birds startle my heart.
The beacon fires have burned for three months;
A letter from home is worth ten thousand gold.
I scratch my white hair, shorter and thinner,
Until it can scarcely hold a pin.

