{"translation":"The wind is sharp, the sky is high, the gibbons cry with grief,
The isle is clear, the sand is white, a lone bird wheels and flies.
Boundless, the rustling leaves come tumbling down,
Endless, the Yangtze rolls and surges on.
A guest for ten thousand miles, I grieve at autumn’s close;
Sick through the better half of life, I climb the terrace alone.
Hardships and bitter regrets have thickened frost upon my temples;
Weary and worn, I have just now put down my cup of turbid wine."}

