translation:
The nation is shattered, yet mountains and rivers remain;
Spring fills the city, where grass and trees grow wild.
Moved by the times, flowers draw our tears;
Grieved by parting, birds startle our hearts.
Beacon fires have burned for three months unbroken;
A letter from home would be worth its weight in gold.
I scratch my white hair, it grows thinner still,
Soon it will be too thin to hold a pin.

