translation:
Wind sharp, sky high, gibbons wail in grief;
Isles clear, sand white, birds wheel in flight.
Boundless, the falling leaves rustle down;
Endless, the Yangtze surges on.
Ten thousand miles a guest in autumn's grief;
A hundred years of ills, I climb the terrace alone.
Hardship and bitter regret have thickened my frosted temples;
Despairing, I have lately stopped my cup of turbid wine.

