translation:
The wind is keen, the sky is high, apes wail their grief;
The islet clear, the sand white, birds wheel and drift.
Boundless, the falling leaves come hissing down;
Endless, the Yangtze surges, rolling on.
A thousand leagues, I grieve at autumn, ever a stranger;
A hundred years, beset with ills, I climb this terrace alone.
Hardship and bitter regret have thickened my frosty temples;
Worn and spent, I have lately set down my cup of turbid wine.

