translation:
A broken state, but hills and streams remain;
Spring in the city, grass and trees run deep.
Moved by the times, flowers bring forth tears;
Hating parting, birds startle the heart.
Beacon fires have burned for three long months;
A letter from home is worth ten thousand gold.
I scratch my white hair, it grows ever thinner,
Soon too scanty to hold a hairpin.

