translation:
The wind is keen, the sky so high, the gibbons' wails are drear;
The isle is clear, the sands are white, birds wheel in endless flight.
Boundless the falling leaves descend with rustling sound;
Endless the Yangtze rolls and surges on without a bound.
Ten thousand miles, in sorrowful autumn, always far from home;
A hundred years, with many ills, I climb this terrace all alone.
Hardship and bitter grief have frosted thick my temples' hair;
Down and out, I've lately ceased the cup of turbid wine to share.

