The kingdom is broken, yet mountains and rivers remain;
In spring, the city is deep with grass and trees.
Moved by the times, flowers bring tears;
Hating parting, birds startle the heart.
Beacon fires have burned for three months;
A family letter is worth ten thousand in gold.
I scratch my white hair, it grows ever thinner;
Soon it will not even hold a hairpin."}

