译文：The wind has stilled, the dust is sweet, the flowers are gone;
The sun is late, and I am weary of combing my head.
Things remain, but the person I loved is gone; all is done.
I wish to speak, but tears flow first instead.

I hear the Double Streams still hold the spring's bright grace;
I thought to drift there in a light boat's low sway.
But I fear those little boats on Double Stream's face
Could never carry all my grief away.

