formatted_result:
{"translation": "Ten years, living and dead both lost in the haze;
Even if I tried not to ponder, I cannot forget.
The lonely grave a thousand miles away,
Nowhere to speak of this desolation.
Even should we meet, you would not know me—
Dust upon my face, temples like frost.

Last night, a vague dream brought me suddenly home;
Through the small window of the pavilion, you were doing your makeup.
We looked at each other, speechless;
Only tears, a thousand lines.
I know that where my heart breaks year after year,
Is the night of the bright moon, the ridge of short pines."}

