{"translation": "Climbing High
By Du Fu

The wind is swift, the sky is high, the gibbons cry with sorrow;
The islet is clear, the sand is white, birds wheel in flight.
Boundless, the falling leaves descend, rustling and rustling;
Endless, the Yangtze rolls on, surging and surging.
Ten thousand miles, grieving at autumn, forever a stranger;\nA hundred years, often ill, I climb this terrace alone.
Hardship and bitterness, I hate how my temples turn frosty white;\nWorn and spent, I have lately stopped my cup of turbid wine."}

